From 743cb0ed2bf1bbc27e2457dbc57170c0b3a0a618 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JoshuaHayesWasHere <josh.hayes121@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:12:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): jstack tree home actions: New child home inline,
 Start a home, New crew task and New scout, Archive

A root home's menu offers New child home: an inline row under the root with the scope's name and
one line on what it owns. Enter sends the root home the user message "Make a scope <name>: owns
<line>.", and the scope shows as starting until its home writes `<scope>/home-id`. A scope the
root home made shows as starting from its plan on disk too, and one only the sidebar asked for
can be dismissed. The name is checked before the send by the rules the root home's "Making a
scope" checks.

A project with no home offers Start a home: a new thread in its main checkout whose first message
is `/home`. Every home offers New crew task and New scout, which put the words in its composer,
after any draft, and open it focused at the end, a composer already mounted included. Archive home
sends the home `/handoff` as a user message, queued after its running turn, and never archives the
T3 thread itself.

The server reports scopes with a plan.md and no home-id or handoff.md as starting, and re-derives the directories
it watches on each refresh, so a scope or a repo home made after it started shows without a
restart.
